\fs28 	N\'91bu resources contain info on the nebulae (or other space phenomena) which are displayed in the background of the star map. These images don\'d5t actually have any effect on events in the game, they\'d5re just there to look pretty. You can, however, combine n\'91bu background images with custom asteroid or interference data in the s\'d8st resources for cool localized effects. The PICT resources associated with the four available n\'91bu resources are numbered 9500-9511, and the effects of the n\'91bu resource\'d5s fields are as follows:\
\
XPos		The image\'d5s position on the star map. These coordinates are\
\
YPos		expressed in the scale of the \'d2normal\'d3 map zoom level (not zoomed in or out) and are relative to the upper-left corner of the image.\
\
\
XSize		The image\'d5s size on the star map. These values are expressed in\
\
YSize		the scale of the \'d2normal\'d3 map zoom level (not zoomed in or out) and tell Override how big to make the image when the map is at normal zoom.}